00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.320 align:start position:0%
today the council agreed its position on  the proposal for new rules on the  conservation of fishery resources and  the protection of marine ecosystems  often referred to as technical measures  the council's general approach aims at  modernizing the existing rules on how  and where fishermen may fish until now  European fishermen have had to respect  more than 30 different regulations which  constitute a particularly complex and  burdensome legislative framework we want  to make their life easier  guarantee legal certainty and focus on  innovation on the Malta meta fish  forever declaration we discussed the  significance of the declaration signed  on the 29th and 30th March in Valletta  our discussion today is also Illustrated  our commitment to actively implement the  Declaration on sustainable development  goal number 14 the sustainable use of  the oceans we discussed the ocean  conference which will be held at DeLand  in June and the other ocean conference  which will be hosted by the EU in Malta  in October and these two conferences are  the most important events for our oceans  this year
 

